{
 "note": "Mutants of the online size limit, the count of the start ants and the heavy-map flag of the list (nothing is refused for ants), the weight of a big map, the words for a game that cannot load a map, the public door's map files, the history of approved maps and the arena's play limits, for tools/mutate.py (docs/WORKFLOW.md, 'Mutation checks'). Run from the checkout with a configured build folder: python3 tools/mutate.py tests/data/online_limit_mutants.json --keep-going --jobs 1 --timeout 900. Every mutant must be caught: each breaks one rule of docs/SERVER.md ('Online size limit', 'The leader's START') or docs/MAP_SUBMISSIONS.md ('Older games and big maps'); the test maps' own rules (the canonical file and its limits) are tests/data/test_maps_mutants.json. Not listed on purpose: the weight of a retired match (no test has a rematch on a big map), the wiring of main.cpp (the program is run by the script suites), and three second locks: the name of the person who left (the room looks at the seat as well), the hash check of load_map_file (the replay's own checkpoints refuse another map) and the cap of the weight when places are counted (a match heavier than all the places only makes the server full).",
